{"created": "2026-11-11T17:24:12.911089+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-11T17:24:13.153072+00:00", "id": 24142496, "conceptrecid": "24142495", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24142496", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.24142495", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24142496", "metadata": {"title": "Offline Reachability in Directed Acyclic Graphs under Vertex Failures", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24142496", "publication_date": "2026-11-11", "description": "<p>We study an offline reachability problem in a directed acyclic graph: given a common source and failure sets paired with target sets, does any query retain a reachable target? This is linearly equivalent to finding a path to a labelled terminal that avoids every vertex forbidding its label. For queries with at most two failures, let V, E, q_b&gt;=1 and M count vertices, arcs, queries and target incidences, and put S=V+E+q_b+M. For every integer tau&gt;=1, our threshold algorithm uses &Otilde;(S+E tau+(V+E)q_b/tau) time and &Otilde;(S+V tau) working words, counting discovery, edge scans and target aggregation. Here &Otilde; suppresses polylogarithmic factors. Setting tau=ceil(sqrt(q_b)) gives &Otilde;(V^(3/2)) time when E, q_b and M are O(V). Exact sharing of identical stored sets preserves the time bound, but can still require superlinear space. Further algorithms give near-linear time if the DAG has polylogarithmic depth or a supplied partition into polylogarithmically many sequences in which each vertex reaches the next. For unrestricted multiplicity, clique and directed-cycle reductions give conditional reachability bounds at specified label-count regimes, distinguishing combinatorial from general word random-access machine algorithms. We also study falsification of guarded Boolean expressions: the listed Hitting Set Conjecture gives a conditional lower bound for falsifying at least one of several shared outputs. Near-linear total time for arbitrary two-failure batches, and near-linear space at the square-root-threshold time bound, remain open.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Shaik, Idris Ali", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["directed acyclic graphs", "reachability", "vertex failures", "dominators", "fine-grained complexity"], "version": "1.0", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "24142495"}}]}}, "title": "Offline Reachability in Directed Acyclic Graphs under Vertex Failures", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24142496", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24142496", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24142496?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24142496", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24142496", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24142496", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24142496/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24142495", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24142495", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24142495", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24142495", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24142496/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24142496/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24142496/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24142496/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24142496:offline-reachability-vertex-failures-v1.0.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24142496:offline-reachability-vertex-failures-v1.0.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24142496:offline-reachability-vertex-failures-v1.0.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24142496:offline-reachability-vertex-failure